# M7 — serialize regular wasm32 .blend files with Blender's canonical historical
# 32-bit (i386) layout while retaining the naturally 8-aligned wasm32 layout for
# live memory and undo memfiles. SDNA does not encode member offsets, so makesdna
# emits both layouts and the writer reconstructs divergent structs field-by-field
# before replacing pointers with stable address identifiers. The same generated
# runtime-offset table serves read/write reconstruction and runtime pointer traversal;
# parsed undo SDNA retains its otherwise-unencoded runtime-layout identity. Native
# generation remains byte-identical.
